[#:seon.task{:name "changed-namespaces-flags-a-namespace-sci-merely-touched"
             :plan "`seon.sci.arm/changed-namespaces` flags a namespace SCI merely touched (an unresolved qualified symbol), so the facts stage refuses a plain call (stale-agent-platform lane; 4be90d597 hid only the diagnostic). Done when the producer no longer reports a touched-only namespace as changed and a regression evaluates a plain call over an unresolved qualified symbol."}
 #:seon.task{:name "arming-prints-the-authored-contract-to-read-it-back"
             :plan "`seon.sci.arm/arm!` hands `seon.sci.eval/install-function-contract!` the Var's :malli/schema as (pr-str contract), and `seon.instrument/wrap-interpreted` reads it back with edn/read-string: a value printed to text and parsed again outside the value printer (kondo's one-printer warning on arm.clj). Correct: pass the contract form as data from the write to the compile; the stored row keeps its text where the store needs it. Proof: the arming path's existing tests (seon.cluster.turn-test/a-changed-arity-redefinition-is-callable-in-the-same-pass, `seon.cluster.turn-test/contracted-redefinition-exactly-replaces-the-entity`) stay green with no pr-str on the arming path."}
 #:seon.task{:name "arming-projection-is-rebuilt-per-caller-within-one-form"
             :plan "When a form registers a schema the batch has not applied yet, `seon.sci.arm/arming-projection` rebuilds the delta projection (`seon.schema/projection-with-declarations`, about 5-8 ms and 10 MB per rebuild on the default program) for each caller in that form: `seon.sci.arm/arm!` once per arming write, `seon.turn.batch/schema-notes` and `seon.turn.batch/derive-form` once each. Repro: (do (`seon.schema/register!` :k [:int]) (defn ^{:malli/schema [:=> [:cat :k] :int]} f [x] x) (defn ^{:malli/schema [:=> [:cat :k] :int]} g [x] x)). Correct: one rebuild per form whose delta changed, the value handed to every reader. Proof: a pass with that form shows one projection-with-declarations call per form in its profile, and seon.cluster.turn-test/a-function-using-a-schema-registered-in-the-same-form-is-admitted stays green."}
 #:seon.task{:name "an-unarmable-contract-breaks-the-definition"
             :plan "A defn whose contract cannot arm stops working: (defn badc {:malli/schema [:=> [:cat :no.such/schema] :int]} [x] x) then (badc 1) answers 'audit.scratch/badc is unavailable: its contract did not arm' on default 2026-10-08, where plain SCI answers 1. `seon.sci.arm/arm!` catches the arming failure and replaces the Var root with refusing-root. CLAUDE.md: preserve malformed contracts as data and never arm them; the owner's law: any valid Clojure SCI can execute works. Correct: the evaluated definition keeps its root, the contract failure is a diagnostic beside it. Proof: a deftest where a defn with an unknown schema key still answers its call and the reply carries the arming diagnostic. Read `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/repl-audit/repl-audit-opus-audit.md`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-fresh-acquisition-restores-the-persisted-imports"
             :plan "Three `seon.cluster.turn-test` deftests are red on HEAD bc347d583 (2026-10-12): `import-addition-is-ordinary-data-and-reacquires-exactly` and `import-only-ns-unmap-installs-exactly-after-its-context-commit` show a fresh acquisition does not restore the agent namespace's persisted import (`(get-in (sci.core/namespace-bindings fresh 'my.agents.agent-a) [:imports 'String])` is nil, and the persisted `ns-unmap` mask is not reinstalled: `(resolve 'String)` still answers `java.lang.String`), and `acquisition-orders-agent-authored-refer-targets-and-ignores-alias-cycles` finds `:seon.sci.eval/installed` 7 where 6 is expected. One cause to find: how `seon.sci.arm` acquisition installs a namespace's imports and refer targets from the database on a fresh context. Done when the three are green. Read `seon.cluster.agent/acquire-context!` and `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-12/red-triage.md`."}]
